      "id": "5881963",
      "refId": "e5da1d6c-c7db-4d37-a9f2-c92fef27f119",
      "header": "Leverage BPMN to Undo Actions",
      "description": "BPMN is an ideal tool for rolling back actions that have been taken during execution of a business process, even in a distributed architecture. Instead of hand-coding rollback logic across multiple microservices, the BPMN compensation event can automatically undo previous tasks.",
      "hideOnOverview": false,
      "position": 1,
      "characteristics": []
    },
    {
      "id": "5881962",
      "refId": "779d0d7b-d6fa-4947-9f75-17103b5113d7",
      "header": "Multi-Channel Communication",
      "description": "This blueprint demonstrates how to communicate through multiple channels and accommodates situations where a person cannot be contacted through more than one channel. The example can be extended to other methods of communication; for example, sending an SMS to a phone number.",
